    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Ship-chandler on Tarpot Lane, and the oldest fence on the Docklands.</strong> Sixty-three. CR 1/2.</p><p>She sold the Gull to the Weigher, and it is the worst thing she has ever done. The Weigher holds the debt of her grandson Kit \u2014 forty gold lions lost at dice in Orgsworth, and the boy's hands if it is not paid \u2014 and the price of the marker was the name of the only customer who had ever lifted her veil in Breck's shop.</p><p><strong>In the Gull's Job</strong> she sells the party tools and a builder's plan of the museum, at the Gull's direction, and then sells the Weigher the night they mean to use them. She is frightened, guilty, quick-tongued and not wicked: she is cornered. The tin soldier on her shelf is Kit's.</p><p><strong>Turning her:</strong> pay Kit's debt (40 gp to the Weigher's clerk at the weigh-house, and she will believe it when she sees the marker), or bring her the Gull's own word that Kit is safe. Either way she will tell the Weigher whatever night the party chooses.</p><p><em>Sheet derived from the Councilor Belven Astor stat block (CR 1/2, 33 hp) \u2014 kit renamed and redescribed.</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
